+- **The review acts (`review_confirm_plan`, `review_decide_premise`, `review_waive_readiness`, `review_waive_coverage`, `review_complete`).** These are cards a person answers, in the shell or in the Telegram topic (one allowed user, once, within an hour; the record keeps `pressedBy` and `pressedAt`). An autonomous (unattended) run has nobody to answer them, so it is excluded from the card gate: it is not given these tools and closes the package through the CLI path as before (`keryx review complete`), while any waiver, which needs a terminal, stops it at the floor. An interactive agent in the shell completes a review only through the `review_complete` card; the terminal commands stay for a human who finishes the package in a terminal.
